            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Years and Introduction to Photography</strong><br>\nAnsel Adams was born in 1902 in San Francisco, California. He first became interested in photography during a family trip to Yosemite National Park at the age of 14. Adams was largely self-taught and read photography magazines, attended camera club meetings, and participated in exhibitions to refine his craft.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Embracing the American Wilderness</strong><br>\nAdams is best known for his black and white landscape photographs of the American West. He captured the vastness and beauty of wilderness areas, including national parks and other protected areas, with a particular focus on the clarity and detail of natural elements.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Development of the Zone System</strong><br>\nAdams, along with Fred Archer, developed the Zone System, a technique that allows photographers to precisely control the exposure and contrast of a photograph. This system was integral to Adams's work and to the field of photography, as it enabled a greater expression of artistic vision.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
