            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Environmental Activism and Preservation</strong><br>\nAdams was an environmentalist who advocated for the preservation of wilderness areas through his photographic work. His images have been used to promote the conservation of nature and have had a lasting impact on environmental awareness and activism.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Publications and Photographic Series</strong><br>\nAdams's work was published extensively, with books such as \"Making a Photograph,\" \"The Negative,\" and \"The Print\" educating generations of photographers. His series of photobooks, including \"Sierra Nevada: The John Muir Trail\" and \"Yosemite and the Range of Light,\" were instrumental in his rise to prominence.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence on the Art of Photography</strong><br>\nAdams's work and his technical mastery of the photographic process influenced the development of photography as a recognized art form. He was a key figure in establishing photography galleries and museum photography departments.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
